[0.482, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[0.039, "o", "\r\n# Case: deslop-release-announcement  with 0.7777777777777777  without 0.6666666666666666\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "```markdown\r\n# fluxcache 1.0\r\n\r\nfluxcache is a semantic cache for LLM API calls that understands prompt meaning, not just exact matches.\r\n\r\nThis release adds a sidecar service mode alongside the Python library, enabling caching across multiple applications and languages. Benchmarks show a 40% reduction in model API calls with a median lookup time of 120 milliseconds.\r\n\r\n14 contributors sent pull requests to this release.\r\n```\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "# fluxcache 1.0\r\n\r\nfluxcache 1.0 is a semantic cache for LLM API calls—it understands prompt meaning, not text matches. This release adds a sidecar service mode alongside the existing Python library, enabling caching across multiple applications and languages.\r\n\r\nBenchmarks show 40% fewer model API calls and 120ms median lookup times. The release was shaped by 14 community contributors who sent pull requests and built a tool that makes LLM applications faster and more cost-effective.\r\n\r\nDeploy as a standalone service or Python library sidecar. fluxcache 1.0 optimizes LLM infrastructure at any scale.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n# Case: launch-announcement  with 0.9444444444444445  without 0.6111111111111112\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "We're releasing fluxcache 1.0. The cache stores responses for LLM API calls and matches prompts by meaning, not exact text, so semantically similar requests reuse cached results. In our benchmarks, this cut model calls by 40% with median lookup latency of 120 ms.\r\n\r\nVersion 1.0 introduces a sidecar service mode that runs alongside the Python library, letting you cache API calls from any application or language. The release represents work from 14 contributors.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "We're excited to announce fluxcache 1.0—a semantic caching solution that dramatically reduces LLM API costs.\r\n\r\nFluxcache caches LLM API calls by matching prompts at the semantic level, not just string matching. In our benchmarks, this approach cut model calls by 40% while maintaining response quality.\r\n\r\nWith version 1.0, we're introducing a sidecar service mode alongside our existing Python library, giving you flexibility in how you integrate caching into your stack. Cached lookups complete in a median of 120ms, adding minimal latency to your applications.\r\n\r\nThis release represents the effort of 14 contributors across the community. We're grateful for everyone who helped shape fluxcache into a production-ready tool for modern LLM workflows.\r\n\r\nGet started with the documentation or explore the GitHub repository.\r\n"]
[0.106, "x", "0"]
